        alt="picture of 3 falafels on a bed of vegetables"
        class="story-image">

    <h3>Our Story</h3>

    <p>At Palmyra, we are passionate about creating delicious and
        healthy food options for our community. Our journey began
        amidst
        the challenges of the Syrian war, driven by a simple idea:
        to
        share the authentic flavors of our cherished family recipes
        with
        busy families and individuals who want to eat well but don't
        have the time or energy to cook. Starting from scratch, we
        have
        crafted a menu that honors our heritage and uses fresh,
        locally-sourced ingredients. With the help of our talented
        team,
        we have transformed this idea into a successful business
        that
        serves hundreds of happy customers every day.
    </p>

</article>

<article class="story-card">

    <img src="images/hummus-img.webp"
        alt="picture of hummus with olives, parsley, and tahini on top"
        class="story-image">

    <h3>Our Philosophy</h3>

    <p>We believe that food should be both delicious and nutritious.
        That's why we use only the freshest ingredients and prepare
        everything from scratch. Our falafel dough is made fresh
        from
        scratch, never imported or frozen, and cooked right away
        with
        freshly ground spices. Our hummus starts from fresh
        chickpeas,
        not canned, ensuring an authentic and vibrant taste. We
        pride
        ourselves on serving fresh food, not fast food. We are
        dedicated
        to conveying the rich culinary heritage of Syria, making it
        accessible to people anytime. Just like in Syria, where
        people
        can stop by and enjoy a light but fresh meal, we offer a
        variety
        of wholesome and flavorful options for those looking for a
        quick
        and healthy lunch, a family dinner, or catering for your
        next
        event. Whether you're craving a taste of home or exploring
        new
        flavors, we have you covered.
    </p>

</article>